    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d927">

                <pb facs="0725" n="609" xml:id="pg609"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13396.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister to Mexico to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-05T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 5, 1914, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>176. Instead of receiving any reply from Foreign Office to my notes sent as per
                    your No. 252, September 22, 9 p.m., and No. 267, October 1, 7 p.m., the papers
                    to-day announced as reported in official circles that they are going to ask the
                    American Government if order for withdrawal from Vera Cruz is still in force and
                    if so to fix a date on which evacuation will take place.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
